3D Controller Models
  Adapted from Handheld Companion (https://github.com/Valkirie/HandheldCompanion)
  The Xbox 360 and Steam Deck bodies, and the 3D view's model and animation
  code. Handheld Companion also documented the Steam Deck report and haptic
  decode, the Steam Controller (2015) power-off report, the handheld daemon
  watch list and the update check timing.
  Copyright (c) CasperH2O, Lesueur Benjamin, trippyone
  Licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
  The DualShock 4, DualSense, DualSense Edge, Xbox Series and Switch 2 Pro
  Controller models are by hado (https://www.cgtrader.com/designers/hado),
  bought on CGTrader under its Royalty Free License.

assettocorsasharedmemory
  https://github.com/mdjarv/assettocorsasharedmemory
  Copyright (c) 2016 Mathias Djärv
  The Assetto Corsa and Competizione static-page struct prefix
  (SPageFileStatic up to MaxRpm) behind the RPM shift LED telemetry.
  Licensed under the MIT License

Bouncy Castle (bc-csharp)
  https://github.com/bcgit/bc-csharp
  Copyright (c) 2000-2025 The Legion of the Bouncy Castle Inc.
  (https://www.bouncycastle.org)
  Cryptography for Remote Link pairing and transport: X25519 key agreement,
  Ed25519 signatures, and ChaCha20-Poly1305.
  Licensed under the Bouncy Castle Licence (an adaptation of the MIT License)

bs2b
  https://github.com/kcat/openal-soft/blob/master/core/bs2b.cpp
  Copyright (c) 2005 Boris Mikhaylov. MIT License. Bauer
  stereophonic-to-binaural crossfeed. PadForge ports the filter to C# for
  headphone output on the controller audio path.

BthPS3 + BthPS3PSM
  https://github.com/nefarius/BthPS3
  Copyright (c) 2018-2026, Nefarius Software Solutions e.U.
  PadForge bundles the Microsoft-attestation-signed BthPS3 profile driver
  and BthPS3PSM filter driver binaries unmodified and installs them on
  demand for DualShock 3 Bluetooth support.
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License (full text at the end of this file)

CommunityToolkit.Mvvm
  https://github.com/CommunityToolkit/dotnet
  Copyright (c) .NET Foundation and Contributors
  Licensed under MIT License

Concentus
  https://github.com/lostromb/concentus
  By Logan Stromberg, with copyrights held by Skype Limited, Xiph.Org
  Foundation, and other Opus contributors. Encodes the Opus frames for
  DualSense speaker audio over Bluetooth.
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License (the Opus license)

DS4AudioStreamer
  https://github.com/nefarius/DS4AudioStreamer
  By nefarius. Reference for the DualShock 4 Bluetooth audio report
  framing (0x14/0x17 layout, frame counter, volume enables). PadForge's
  SBC encoder is an original C# implementation from the public
  Bluetooth A2DP specification and contains no libsbc (GPL) code.
  Licensed under MIT License

ds4mac
  https://github.com/khallmark/ds4mac
  By khallmark. DualShock 4 audio protocol documentation (SBC
  parameters, packet layouts, Bluetooth-only audio finding). Read as
  documentation only. PadForge's implementation is original C# and
  contains no GPL code.
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License v2.0

DS5_Bridge
  https://github.com/SundayMoments/DS5_Bridge
  By SundayMoments. Behavioral reference for jack-detect audio
  routing (the Follow Headphone Jack mode's switch-on-plug pattern)
  and for one-sink-at-a-time Bluetooth audio routing. Read as
  documentation only. PadForge's implementation is original C# and
  contains no AGPL code.
  Licensed under AGPL-3.0

DsHidMini
  https://github.com/nefarius/DsHidMini
  Copyright (c) 2020-2025, Benjamin Höglinger-Stelzer
  DualShock 3 protocol reference: sixpair feature reports, Bluetooth
  output-report template, enable ordering, battery status map.
  PadForge's implementation is original C#.
  Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License

duaLib
  https://github.com/WujekFoliarz/duaLib
  By WujekFoliarz. The DualSense output-report byte map and Sony's
  scePad semantics (LightFadeAnimation, validFlag bit roles, the
  volume windows, audio output paths, and the reconnect re-arm
  discipline) that ground PadForge's DualSense effect and audio
  writers. PadForge's implementation is original C#.
  Licensed under MIT License

dualsense-bt-haptics
  https://github.com/awalol/dualsense-bt-haptics
  By awalol. The HeadsetPlayMusic tool documented the Opus framing and
  packet layout PadForge's Bluetooth speaker stream re-implements.
  Licensed under MIT License

dualsense-tester
  https://github.com/daidr/dualsense-tester (https://ds.daidr.me/)
  Copyright (c) 2023 Xuezhou Dai (daidr)
  Reference for the Sony Bluetooth feature-report CRC framing and the
  vendor test commands PadForge forwards from virtual to physical pads.
  Licensed under MIT License

DualSenseY-v2
  https://github.com/WujekFoliarz/DualSenseY-v2
  By WujekFoliarz. Behavioral reference for USB controller audio
  passthrough and adaptive trigger effects. No license published.
  PadForge's implementation is original C#.

DualShock 3 Bluetooth research
  ScpToolkit (https://github.com/nefarius/ScpToolkit), sixad
  (https://github.com/RetroPie/sixad), and transbt
  (https://github.com/null-dev/transbt) were read as protocol
  documentation only. All three are GPL-licensed. PadForge's pairing and
  reader code is original C# and contains no GPL code.

Fusion
  https://github.com/xioTechnologies/Fusion
  Copyright (c) 2021 x-io Technologies
  The tilt-compensated compass heading behind compass yaw is a C# port of
  FusionCompass, and the yaw correction uses Fusion's default AHRS gain.
  Licensed under the MIT License

GamepadMotionHelpers
  https://github.com/JibbSmart/GamepadMotionHelpers
  By JibbSmart. The player-space and world-space gyro conversions and
  the Gyro Tilt gravity update are adapted for C#.
  Licensed under the MIT License

GestureSign
  https://github.com/TransposonY/GestureSign
  By TransposonY. The touchpad angular-margin scoring follows the algorithm
  its PointPatternAnalyzer describes. GestureSign was read for the algorithm
  only, and PadForge's implementation is original C# with no GPL code.
  Licensed under the GNU General Public License v2.0

HelixToolkit
  https://github.com/helix-toolkit/helix-toolkit
  Copyright (c) 2022 Helix Toolkit contributors
  Licensed under MIT License

