Kaldi, OpenFst, OpenBLAS and CLAPACK
  https://github.com/alphacep/kaldi (Kaldi, Copyright the Kaldi authors,
  listed in its COPYING file)
  https://github.com/alphacep/openfst (OpenFst, Copyright 2005-2020 Google LLC)
  https://github.com/OpenMathLib/OpenBLAS (OpenBLAS 0.3.20, Copyright (c)
  2011-2014, The OpenBLAS Project)
  https://github.com/alphacep/clapack (CLAPACK 3.2.1, Copyright (c)
  1992-2008 The University of Tennessee)
  The speech decoder, the transducer library and the linear algebra that
  libvosk is made of. All four are linked statically into libvosk.dll, in
  the x64 one Alpha Cephei builds and in the ARM64 one built here. CLAPACK
  is Fortran translated to C, and it brings the f2c runtime into the link
  with it (libf2c, Copyright 1990 - 1997 by AT&T, Lucent Technologies and
  Bellcore).
  Kaldi and OpenFst are licensed under the Apache License 2.0. OpenBLAS and
  CLAPACK are licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License. libf2c carries a
  notice of its own (full texts below)

